WEBVTT

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:06.400
I will stop at nothing to win.

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:09.650
I will put everything I have into these lies.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:14.280
The committee to conquer Steel 
Lady Nanase is now in session!

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.120
<b>Does Steel Lady Nanase truly exist?</b>

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:55.550
Does Steel Lady Nanase truly exist?

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:59.010
Or is she a fictional being 
existing only in rumors,

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:01.510
who was created by 
someone for some reason?

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:05.430
Isn't she just an urban legend?

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:06.640
Name: kuebiko 09/04 22:15 ID.Mmimn
Does Steel Lady Nanase truly exist?
Or is she a fictional being existing only in rumors, 
who was created by someone for some reason?
 Isn't she just an urban legend?

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:09.520
Saki-san.

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:13.910
Please let me know if there is any 
significant change with Kuro-senpai.

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:17.320
All right. For now, he's managing to 
defend himself against Steel Lady Nanase

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:18.990
without getting killed.

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:22.610
<i>Until yesterday, all the talk 
about Steel Lady Nanase was</i>

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:28.320
<i>"Someone told me they saw her," or 
"Someone told me they were attacked."</i>

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:31.580
<i>But today, there's been a big change.</i>

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:35.810
<i>There was an incident where 
a detective named Terada was</i>

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:37.980
<i>killed by someone believed 
to be Steel Lady Nanase.</i>

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:42.300
<i>The location is Makurazaka City. 
The time was the middle of the night.</i>

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.560
<i>Despite getting his face smashed in,</i>

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:48.310
<i>there were no signs that 
the detective resisted.</i>

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:52.190
<b>Active Duty Detective Found Dead</b>

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:52.190
<b>The victim, Sergeant Terada Tokunosuke</b>

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:52.190
<i>The cause of death that was 
announced was the blow to his face.</i>

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:55.810
<i>So, yes, unless something 
like Steel Lady Nanase</i>

00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:58.250
<i>had hit him in the face 
with a steel beam,</i>

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:00.570
<i>it's hard to believe anyone 
would die like that.</i>

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:03.070
Name: kuebiko 09/04 22:16 ID.Mmimn43
 The location is Makurazaka City. The time was the middle of the night. Despite getting his face smashed in, there were no signs that the detective resisted. The cause of death that was announced was the blow to his face.
Despite the fact that this detective named Terada was big and had judo training, he was easily killed. So, yes, unless something like Steel Lady Nanase had hit him in the face with a steel beam, it's hard to believe anyone would die like that.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:09.000
The location is Makurazaka City. The time was the middle of the night. Despite getting his face smashed in, there were no signs that the detective resisted. The cause of death that was announced was the blow to his face.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:09.960
Name: Anonymous 09/04 22:18 Id.mvtg
But that just means Steel Lady Nanase 
was responsible for that incident, right?

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:12.630
<i>No.</i>

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:15.390
<i>That's what the killer wanted you to believe.</i>

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:23.210
<i>That's exactly why the killer 
needed Steel Lady Nanase.</i>

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:28.250
<i>In order to murder Detective Terada, 
the killer created</i>

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:30.890
<i>an urban legend called Steel Lady Nanase.</i>

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:34.150
They made up a ghost that has no way

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:35.710
of actually existing.

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:43.580
<i>Now... Let's see how many will latch on.</i>

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:57.370
Detective Terada was very good at his job.

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:01.290
He always kept his eye on 
the changes within the city,

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:03.680
so he sensed when a crime 
was going to happen,

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:07.090
and he wanted to take action 
before the incident got out of hand.

00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:09.430
He was an excellent detective.

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:12.690
That's what the killer 
tried to take advantage of.

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:15.690
There was an urban legend 
from Makurazaka City

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:17.960
going around in a small 
community on the Internet.

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:20.440
<b>Steel Lady Nanase Wiki</b>

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:20.440
By taking advantage of the 
monster, Steel Lady Nanase,

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:23.900
they were able to commit the actual 
crimes and attempted crimes

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:25.570
one after another.

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:29.860
The killer dressed up the way 
Steel Lady Nanase was perceived

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:31.580
and attacked people night after night.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:34.830
They made their steel beam 
from either wood or Styrofoam,

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:37.840
and padded their chest 
to attract attention.

00:04:38.390 --> 00:04:40.390
With black paint on part of their face,

00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:43.340
it would probably look smashed 
in when seen at night.

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:45.340
Then there's the large bow in their hair.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:47.890
Witnesses wouldn't have 
time to confirm it all,

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:51.060
so they'll think her face had been smashed in.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:52.810
Is that actually believable?

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:54.950
It may not be.

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:56.800
This is a lie, after all.

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:58.810
It just needs to be somewhat believable.

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:00.070
Name: kuebiko 09/04 22:25 ID.Mmimn4
With black paint on part of their face, it would probably look smashed in when seen at night. Then there's the large bow in their hair. Witnesses wouldn't have time to confirm it all, so they'll think her face had been smashed in.

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:02.070
Name: kuebiko 09/04 22:25 ID.Mmimn43
 And then the killer waited for statements like "I was attacked by Steel Lady Nanase" to spread, not just as a rumor, but in reports taken to the police.

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:04.450
And then the killer waited for statements like

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:06.570
"I was attacked by Steel Lady Nanase" to spread,

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:08.820
not just as a rumor, 
but in reports taken to the police.

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:12.080
But the police didn't immediately 
take this seriously.

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:15.580
And I'm sure many victims had second 
thoughts about turning in a police report.

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:20.110
But if incidents like that start 
occurring all over the city,

00:05:20.110 --> 00:05:23.460
wouldn't a good detective think something 
was going on and take action?

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:27.500
<i>Maybe someone is acting like 
a monster from an urban legend</i>

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:30.490
<i>named Steel Lady Nanase 
as part of some plot.</i>

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:34.370
<i>Given all the work they're putting into this, 
it can't be dismissed as a mere prank.</i>

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:36.730
<i>They might actually be planning some crime.</i>

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:38.580
That thought crossed his mind,

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:40.610
so he began investigating 
the incident on his own.

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:46.530
<b>Traffic Safety</b>

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:44.380
This is exactly what the killer wanted.

00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:48.250
If Detective Terada started investigating 
Steel Lady Nanase on his own,

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:51.310
they'd be able to get the detective alone.

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:57.650
The killer was able to create a time frame 
where the detective would be on his own.

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:01.590
<b>Anonymous</b>

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:01.590
<i>Too long. I don't have time to read this.</i>

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:03.440
<b>Anonymous</b>

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:03.540
<i>What are you basing this on?</i>

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:06.670
<b>Anon</b>

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:05.710
<i>Steel Lady Nanase is real!</i>

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:05.880
<b>Anonymous</b>

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:07.220
<b>Anon</b>

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:08.860
<i>There's no logical explanation other 
than that it was really a ghost.</i>

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:07.220
<b>Anonymous</b>

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:07.220
<b>Nameless</b>

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:11.550
<i>Let's hear them out a little longer.</i>

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:16.230
<b>Anonymous</b>

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:16.230
<i>I'm sure there are some people 
here who don't believe in ghosts.</i>

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:21.230
And then the killer contacted 
Detective Terada.

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:25.240
What's up?

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:26.250
<i>Terada-san!</i>

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:28.810
<i>I was just attacked by Steel Lady Nanase!</i>

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:31.450
<i>They ran off,</i>

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:34.490
but they dropped their weapon and bow.

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:37.760
There are also some footprints left 
here, so I'd like you to come.

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:41.970
I'm not sure of everything yet, 
so I'd prefer if you came alone.

00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:43.210
That's likely all it took

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:47.090
for Detective Terada to 
rush over there on his own.

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:50.180
And the place he was called to 
ended up being the scene of the crime,

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:52.220
the abandoned gas station.

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:54.660
If he was called like that,

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:58.190
Terada-san might've really gone to an 
abandoned gas station alone, but...

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:02.130
Before Detective Terada showed up,

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:05.610
the killer rigged a few things 
at the abandoned gas station.

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:09.490
They hung a huge pendulum from the roof,

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:12.360
attached a rope to the hook on the roof,

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:14.150
and tied a weight at the bottom.

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:17.390
The weight had to be heavy enough

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:21.550
that it could crack someone's 
head open with one swing.

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:25.130
And it needed to swing at

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:29.180
Detective Terada's height, which the 
killer had researched previously.

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.890
Once they had all that done,

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:34.890
the killer would keep the rope extended,

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:37.600
take the end of the pendulum 
that had the weight on it,

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:41.060
and set the weight on the other 
hook set up on the roof.

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:49.360
But this hook could be undone 
at any time by remote control.

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:52.860
Once that hook was undone...

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:55.820
the weight would come flying 
down at incredible speed.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:08:00.250
This is so much work just to kill one person.

00:08:02.570 --> 00:08:05.390
The killer would have Detective 
Terada stand in the spot

00:08:05.390 --> 00:08:06.750
they had previously chosen.

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:09.230
It's not that difficult.

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:13.650
The killer was holding something 
of interest to Detective Terada.

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:16.760
If they waited with that in hand 
at the abandoned gas station,

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:20.270
Detective Terada would stop 
his car near the killer.

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:22.740
Here's the bow that she dropped.

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:25.650
And there are still footprints over there.

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:28.400
It's a bit dark, so I'll go on ahead

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:30.770
and turn on some lights 
so that you don't trip.

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:32.580
Please wait here.

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:33.610
Sure.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:37.940
That's probably all it took to get 
Detective Terada to stand there.

00:08:38.570 --> 00:08:44.710
At that moment, the killer undid the hook 
holding the weight by remote control.

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:50.140
The weight being held by the 
rope would act as a pendulum,

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:52.670
swing across the dark, abandoned gas station,

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:54.650
and split open Detective Terada's head

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:57.300
in a single blow, since he 
was standing in its path.

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:01.710
There were no homes near the scene, 
and cars rarely drove by,

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:05.050
so no one would've spotted 
the rigged pendulum easily.

00:09:06.090 --> 00:09:09.130
Detective Terada wouldn't see 
the pendulum set up to kill him

00:09:09.130 --> 00:09:11.270
until it was too late.

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:17.320
I see... This explains that mystery.

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:20.380
This is how a strong and outstanding detective

00:09:20.380 --> 00:09:23.330
was killed so easily without a struggle.

00:09:23.990 --> 00:09:25.820
There was no way he could predict that

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:27.650
he'd suddenly be attacked by a pendulum,

00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:30.090
so he'd defenselessly get 
his head cracked open.

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:34.590
After murdering Detective Terada, 
the killer puts the setup away.

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:38.840
They remove any trace of them ever 
being there and then flee the scene.

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:43.390
All that's left after that is to 
burn the costume they used

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:46.040
as Steel Lady Nanase, 
along with the pendulum rig.

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:50.210
<i>But the scene is right 
next to the expressway.</i>

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:52.730
<b>Nameless</b>

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:52.730
<i>There's no telling when a car would pass by.</i>

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:57.360
<i>Wouldn't that make this whole convoluted 
setup for a murder kind of risky?</i>

00:09:57.900 --> 00:10:00.180
The killer had researched 
traffic in that area

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:03.820
and knew that very few cars pass 
by during the chosen time period.

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:07.610
They experimented with the pendulum

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:09.790
to determine where Detective 
Terada should stand

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:14.030
and researched everything months prior 
to ensure this setup would work.

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:18.760
<i>The detective died after 
being struck in the face.</i>

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:25.720
<b>Anon</b>

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:21.790
<i>Even if it was dark and hard to see,</i>

00:10:21.790 --> 00:10:24.110
<i>would the killer really go to the 
trouble of rigging a pendulum</i>

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:25.720
<i>that would hit him in the face?</i>

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:31.480
<b>Anon</b>

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:29.670
<i>If they were going to set this up, 
wouldn't they have the detective stand</i>

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:31.480
<b>Anonymous</b>

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:31.480
<i>where the weight would 
strike him from behind?</i>

00:10:31.990 --> 00:10:33.670
<i>If it was coming from the front,</i>

00:10:33.670 --> 00:10:36.490
<i>he might see it and try to dodge 
or guard his face with his hands.</i>

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:41.180
<b>Anon</b>

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:42.870
Precisely. The killer's pendulum setup

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:47.230
was originally rigged so that the 
weight would strike the detective

00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:49.120
from behind, so he wouldn't see it.

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:54.130
But Detective Terada noticed that something 
seemed to be coming toward him.

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:57.230
He may have been unarmed, 
but he was an outstanding detective.

00:10:57.230 --> 00:11:00.510
He might've sensed the 
killer trying to kill him.

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:04.760
He might have even heard 
the hook being released.

00:11:06.210 --> 00:11:08.850
That's why he instinctively 
turned that way.

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:12.270
But the weight was coming at high speed,

00:11:13.050 --> 00:11:17.030
and it was dark. It was too late 
for him to dodge or guard his face.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:23.030
That's why Detective Terada died by getting 
smacked in the face by the weapon.

00:11:23.510 --> 00:11:25.460
You come up with these things so fast.

00:11:26.550 --> 00:11:31.270
<b>Anon</b>

00:11:26.940 --> 00:11:31.270
<i>So was the blow to his face accidental, 
or was it what the killer wanted?</i>

00:11:31.770 --> 00:11:33.500
It's hard to be certain 
one way or another.

00:11:34.070 --> 00:11:37.380
For the killer to intentionally have 
Detective Terada hit in the face,

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:40.300
after dropping the weight 
with the remote,

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:39.380
Look!

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:42.620
they draw his attention 
toward something.

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:46.270
If the killer looked in a certain direction,

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:50.020
there's a good chance that Detective Terada 
would do the same and look that way.

00:11:50.290 --> 00:11:54.900
<b>Anonymous</b>

00:11:50.530 --> 00:11:53.240
<i>Wouldn't that method involve some risks?</i>

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:54.900
Yes. In this case, there's a possibility

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:58.530
that Detective Terada's head would move 
away from the path of the weight.

00:11:58.530 --> 00:12:03.860
That's one con, but the victim dying 
with a blow to the face is a pro.

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:07.030
It's hard to say which the killer chose.

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:12.540
What can be said is that the end result 
was indeed what the killer wanted.

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:14.670
<b>Anonymous</b>

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:14.670
All right, I understand the trick.

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:17.540
<b>Anonymous</b>

00:12:15.010 --> 00:12:17.540
<i>But you haven't explained 
one very important thing.</i>

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:18.860
<i>That's right.</i>

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:21.990
<i>Why did the killer bother 
going to all that trouble?</i>

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:26.140
<i>Not to mention, using the urban 
legend of Steel Lady Nanase itself</i>

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:29.600
<i>as a cover for murder is also a hassle.</i>

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:33.560
<i>Even if the detective was outstanding, 
they could've tried to poison him.</i>

00:12:34.260 --> 00:12:37.260
<i>Rather than preparing Steel Lady 
Nanase's costume and a pendulum,</i>

00:12:37.260 --> 00:12:39.570
<i>it's far easier to just obtain poison.</i>

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:44.320
<i>That's a good point. Why would 
they bother using that trick?</i>

00:12:44.770 --> 00:12:47.400
<i>This lie isn't very persuasive.</i>

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:49.900
The reason the killer 
went to so much trouble

00:12:49.900 --> 00:12:51.580
is that if Detective Terada was killed,

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:55.080
they wanted to distance themselves from 
the investigation as much as possible.

00:12:55.910 --> 00:12:58.320
If an able-bodied detective 
was killed out in the open

00:12:58.320 --> 00:12:59.710
by being struck in the face,

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:03.090
the proposed description of the suspect 
would probably be very biased.

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:05.960
If they couldn't figure out the trick,

00:13:05.960 --> 00:13:09.220
they'd suspect a male who had equal or more 
physical strength than Detective Terada,

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:12.500
and who was probably 
an acquaintance of his.

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:15.980
Meaning the killer is the exact 
opposite of this description.

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:18.710
They are weaker than Detective Terada

00:13:18.710 --> 00:13:21.380
and could not hit him with that much force.

00:13:21.380 --> 00:13:23.690
Someone it would seem unnatural for him

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:26.020
to be alone with in the middle of the night.

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:29.740
If they had killed him with poison,

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:34.170
it would seem like an obvious method 
for them to use to kill him.

00:13:34.590 --> 00:13:35.760
Which means...

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:38.000
the killer is a woman!

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:47.880
The Committee to Conquer Steel Lady Nanase

00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:50.490
If the killer was a woman,

00:13:50.490 --> 00:13:52.100
it would seem unlikely that she'd be

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:54.220
meeting a man in the middle of 
the night in such a secluded area

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:55.890
unless they were dating.

00:13:57.210 --> 00:13:58.700
It also seems unlikely that

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:02.210
she'd be strong enough to kill him by smacking 
him in the face before he could retaliate.

00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:05.900
Detective Terada was an 
acclaimed judo athlete.

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:08.300
There's no way he'd be
easily killed by a woman.

00:14:08.300 --> 00:14:09.230
Yeah.

00:14:08.770 --> 00:14:11.780
That would allow the killer 
to escape the investigation.

00:14:09.230 --> 00:14:10.340
I knew it.

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:16.660
That's why they created a 
ghost like Steel Lady Nanase!

00:14:17.030 --> 00:14:19.630
<i>Why did the killer 
need Steel Lady Nanase,</i>

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:22.010
<i>and why did they use such a 
specific way of killing him?</i>

00:14:22.010 --> 00:14:23.970
<i>This should explain that.</i>

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:25.840
If we can figure out why they used

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:29.220
that setup for the murder and created 
the Steel Lady Nanase incidents,

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:32.050
that will help us narrow 
down the possible suspects.

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:37.180
The killer was able to find out 
Detective Terada's height.

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:40.440
The killer was able to summon 
Detective Terada in the

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:42.940
middle of the night without 
it seeming suspicious.

00:14:43.470 --> 00:14:46.570
The killer was able to predict that 
Detective Terada would make a move

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:49.950
if he noticed something 
strange going on in the city.

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:53.580
Our killer is someone who 
fits all these descriptions.

00:14:54.020 --> 00:14:55.340
The killer...

00:14:57.420 --> 00:15:01.380
is a female police officer stationed at the 
same department as Detective Terada!

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:06.750
If they work at the same department,

00:15:06.750 --> 00:15:08.630
it'd be easy to find out the victim's height,

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:12.450
as well as where his head would 
be in relation to, say, a door.

00:15:13.770 --> 00:15:15.140
If they worked in the same department,

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:17.140
they'd know Detective 
Terada's reputation, as well.

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:19.170
If they're a police officer,

00:15:19.170 --> 00:15:20.960
after supposedly being attacked by a suspect,

00:15:20.960 --> 00:15:22.870
they'd know how to properly 
preserve evidence,

00:15:22.870 --> 00:15:25.270
and no one would suspect 
anything if they contacted

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:27.140
a detective they could rely on.

00:15:28.050 --> 00:15:31.260
The description of the killer 
that comes from all these factors

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:33.020
can only be a female police officer.

00:15:33.810 --> 00:15:36.280
We'll just have to imagine 
her motive, though.

00:15:36.890 --> 00:15:40.090
Perhaps the victim was pursuing 
the killer romantically,

00:15:40.090 --> 00:15:41.670
and she was troubled by that.

00:15:42.090 --> 00:15:46.290
If we were to consider the trouble to 
set everything up, as well as the fact

00:15:46.620 --> 00:15:48.330
that she went so far as to kill him,

00:15:48.330 --> 00:15:50.890
the motive could have come from 
an obsessive web of emotions.

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:55.050
<i>That should cover everything 
for my first claim.</i>

00:15:55.630 --> 00:15:58.170
Steel Lady Nanase is not a ghost.

00:15:58.170 --> 00:16:00.220
She was created by a female police officer

00:16:00.220 --> 00:16:03.400
who made society believe in her existence 
so that she could murder Detective Terada.

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:05.650
In other words, she is a means to a murder.

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:11.030
<i>Even without naming the killer,</i>

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:13.420
<i>she was able to convince 
everyone that the killer</i>

00:16:13.420 --> 00:16:16.280
<i>could exist just by narrowing 
down the possible suspects.</i>

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:19.290
<i>By creating such a detailed 
description of the killer,</i>

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:21.620
<i>she basically narrowed 
down who they could be.</i>

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:22.290
<855> Name: Anonymous 09/04 22:50 ID.Hkeoppq
That seems like a valid reason

00:16:22.930 --> 00:16:25.230
And just like that, the flow of 
the forum completely changed.

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:36.080
<i>Kuro-kun must be working to find a future</i>

00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:38.610
<i>where everyone supports 
Iwanaga-san's solution.</i>

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:45.400
Wait a minute!

00:16:45.820 --> 00:16:48.650
That suspect is basically me!

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:50.500
Oh, so you noticed.

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:52.390
Did you think I wouldn't?!

00:16:53.090 --> 00:16:54.970
A female officer who worked at the same

00:16:54.970 --> 00:16:57.310
police department, and someone
Terada-san had feelings for...

00:16:57.310 --> 00:17:00.220
Even the chief could figure 
that out in one guess!

00:17:00.220 --> 00:17:01.530
You'll just have to bear with me.

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:05.670
I can't just frame a random 
female police officer.

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:08.590
Besides, this solution 
won't hold for much longer.

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:09.290
Huh?

00:17:09.890 --> 00:17:12.130
<i>I don't agree.</i>

00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:13.940
<i>I have to question if a lone female killer</i>

00:17:13.940 --> 00:17:18.360
<i>could've set up the pendulum trick 
by herself on the gas station roof.</i>

00:17:18.360 --> 00:17:21.700
<i>Would it really be safe to make 
up an urban legend big enough</i>

00:17:21.700 --> 00:17:26.040
<i>to cause trouble in the city and make 
Detective Terada take action?</i>

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:27.850
<i>Yeah, I don't see the 
pendulum thing happening.</i>

00:17:28.320 --> 00:17:30.130
Wait, why did the flow change again?

00:17:30.130 --> 00:17:32.210
I know the solution's not that realistic,

00:17:32.210 --> 00:17:35.240
but it's odd that they'd change 
their minds again so quickly.

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:39.500
Didn't the flow just change 
because of Kuro-kun's ability?

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:43.250
Iwanaga-san,

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:46.930
the one who's trying to give Steel Lady 
Nanase a form is Rikka-san, right?

00:17:46.930 --> 00:17:47.500
Yes.

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:49.860
And she has the same ability as Kuro-kun

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:52.380
that allows her to choose the future, right?

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:54.760
Yes. Just as I explained earlier.

00:17:55.830 --> 00:18:00.510
That means Rikka-san can also
force the future she wants.

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:04.390
Yes. And that's exactly why the 
tides turned so quickly again.

00:18:05.540 --> 00:18:08.140
The idea that this is all caused 
by a ghost is a popular view.

00:18:08.890 --> 00:18:11.610
All she had to do was point out 
a few flaws in our solution,

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:16.220
then die once, and she could easily 
shift the flow back in her favor.

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:19.630
It's very possible that a number

00:18:19.630 --> 00:18:22.450
of the posts are being 
written by Rikka-san herself.

00:18:23.970 --> 00:18:24.740
Ri...

00:18:33.590 --> 00:18:37.980
This site itself has many people 
reading and posting at the same time,

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:43.500
but the server isn't going down, 
and we haven't really run into any trolls.

00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:46.350
That's not exactly normal, is it?

00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:51.390
So Rikka-san is probably choosing 
the future with the fewest problems

00:18:51.390 --> 00:18:52.980
and maintaining the site.

00:18:53.540 --> 00:18:55.800
She may not be censoring the posts,

00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:58.490
but she clearly has an advantage.

00:18:59.180 --> 00:19:01.430
<i>Rikka-san also surpasses the laws of nature.</i>

00:19:01.430 --> 00:19:04.270
<i>That means the way to solve 
this hasn't changed at all.</i>

00:19:04.780 --> 00:19:06.610
<i>In fact, because Rikka-san got a head start</i>

00:19:06.610 --> 00:19:09.730
<i>and had everyone believe that a 
ghost named Steel Lady Nanase exists,</i>

00:19:09.730 --> 00:19:11.100
<i>we're at a disadvantage.</i>

00:19:11.940 --> 00:19:13.990
This assembly is unique.

00:19:13.990 --> 00:19:16.500
The truth never existed here.

00:19:16.500 --> 00:19:19.010
All that's here is fiction.

00:19:22.970 --> 00:19:27.520
Both Rikka-san and I know that 
Steel Lady Nanase didn't exist before.

00:19:27.920 --> 00:19:31.900
But she is still trying to 
give that fiction a form.

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:35.520
Meanwhile, Kuro-senpai and I 
are trying to get everyone to

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:38.270
believe the fiction that 
Steel Lady Nanase doesn't exist.

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:53.370
In other words, this is a 
committee of dueling fictions.

00:20:00.060 --> 00:20:01.420
I will win.

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:06.430
I've only used one solution out 
of four that I have so far.

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:09.430
All I need is for part of the 
assembly to believe it.

00:20:09.760 --> 00:20:10.940
Part of it...

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:12.800
<i>I see.</i>

00:20:12.800 --> 00:20:15.440
<i>The Internet is just a swirling 
mass of different views and values.</i>

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:20.400
<i>It's not easy for everyone 
to believe in a single truth.</i>

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:26.930
<i>In that case, you need a variety of 
truths to match the variety of views.</i>

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:30.940
<i>We couldn't completely turn around 
everyone's belief in Steel Lady Nanase</i>

00:20:30.940 --> 00:20:32.690
<i>with the pendulum solution,</i>

00:20:32.690 --> 00:20:35.670
<i>but at least a few of them 
should have some doubt now.</i>

00:20:36.810 --> 00:20:40.260
<i>She's going to repeat this 
process three more times...</i>

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:44.010
<i>to try to chip away at 
Steel Lady Nanase's support.</i>

00:20:44.620 --> 00:20:46.760
<i>Even if she doesn't gain the 
majority with one theory,</i>

00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:50.620
<i>she just has to make them believe 
that Rikka-san's proposed bill</i>

00:20:50.620 --> 00:20:52.300
<i>is not worth voting for.</i>

00:20:53.090 --> 00:20:54.890
<i>That's why this strategy has a chance.</i>

00:20:58.460 --> 00:20:59.900
<i>This girl is unbelievable.</i>

00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:02.350
<i>She's using every bit of her knowledge 
to wield a blade in one hand</i>

00:21:02.350 --> 00:21:04.900
<i>while injecting poison with the other.</i>

00:21:05.620 --> 00:21:08.100
<i>To think that someone 
who's decided to use lies</i>

00:21:08.100 --> 00:21:10.190
<i>as her weapon could be so diabolical...</i>

00:21:12.560 --> 00:21:16.250
<i>No. Steel Lady Nanase is a real ghost.</i>

00:21:12.560 --> 00:21:17.540
<b>Nameless</b>

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:17.540
<i>I saw her with my own eyes!</i>

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:20.330
<i>She appeared in front of 
my car out of nowhere!</i>

00:21:20.330 --> 00:21:22.170
<i>This happened five days ago.</i>

00:21:22.730 --> 00:21:28.100
<i>She appeared like smoke, went berserk, 
and started swinging a steel beam at me!</i>

00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:41.350
<i>That was definitely a vengeful spirit.</i>

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:44.650
<b>Nameless</b>

00:21:41.350 --> 00:21:44.650
<i>I could've been killed like that detective!</i>

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:51.620
I'm going to win.

00:22:05.690 --> 00:22:06.620
All right,

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:09.050
let's commence solution number two!

00:22:11.930 --> 00:22:16.160
To Be Continued

00:23:44.880 --> 00:23:46.860
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:46.860 --> 00:23:50.970
We deploy the second and third solutions 
to defeat Steel Lady Nanase.

00:23:50.970 --> 00:23:53.690
However, Sakuragawa Rikka stands in our way.
